import{_ as o,o as t,c as r,a5 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Image + prompt video worker","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/i2v-worker-integration/spec.md","filePath":"feature/i2v-worker-integration/spec.md"}'),i={name:"feature/i2v-worker-integration/spec.md"};function n(d,e,s,c,p,l){return t(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="image-prompt-video-worker" tabindex="-1">Image + prompt video worker <a class="header-anchor" href="#image-prompt-video-worker" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Image + prompt video worker&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Objective: connect BrandHub&#39;s existing AI video web request to the user&#39;s Qwen-edit + Wan-I2V worker. Uploading an image and a prompt must work without a motion-reference video.</p><p>User story: the creator chooses image + prompt, supplies an image and request, selects 5/10/15/20 seconds, and receives a playable stored video through the current async job UI.</p><p>Acceptance criteria:</p><ul><li>Keep the worker key in AI Service <code>.env</code>, never in frontend assets or checked-in files.</li><li>Use separate <code>I2V_WORKER_URL</code> and <code>I2V_WORKER_API_KEY</code>; preserve existing Qwen image and Tuấn Animate worker settings.</li><li>For requests with an image, no pose video and I2V configured, submit multipart <code>reference_image</code>, <code>image_prompt</code>, <code>motion_prompt</code>, <code>duration_seconds</code>, width and height to <code>/api/v1/generate_video</code> with <code>X-API-Key</code>.</li><li>Poll <code>/api/v1/jobs/{prompt_id}</code>. If the worker has no S3 URL, fetch authenticated <code>/api/v1/media</code> and store the MP4 using the backend&#39;s existing S3 uploader.</li><li>Preserve pose-reference Animate requests and text-only Veo requests.</li><li>Invalid duration, missing image/key and upstream errors must fail clearly; do not silently round duration or fall back to a paid provider after worker rejection.</li><li>i18n: add matching <code>editor.studio.video.generationMode</code>, <code>imagePromptMode</code>, <code>referenceMode</code>, <code>promptHint</code>, <code>promptTooShort</code>, <code>aspectRatioLabel</code>, <code>portrait</code>, <code>landscape</code> keys in vi/en editor locales. Reuse existing brief/duration keys.</li><li>Light/dark: reuse existing theme tokens for select, textarea and labels; no new palette, layout or modal.</li></ul><p>API contract: the public web/business video contract remains unchanged; an image-only request already supports prompt, referenceImageBase64, durationSeconds and aspectRatio. The AI Service adapts those fields to the new worker.</p><p>UI states: image-prompt mode defaults to 5 seconds and portrait; reference mode retains its measured-duration UI. Existing pending, processing, complete and failed states continue to work.</p><p>Edge cases: worker restart/unknown job, key 401, unsupported 8-second requests, completed job without MP4, local-only worker output, empty prompt. Out of scope: product-video storyboard pipeline, worker model changes, AWS credential changes, deployment, GPU renders and credit-policy changes.</p><p>Definition of done: focused adapter/config tests pass, frontend lint/type checks pass, URL/key verified by authenticated read-only health; report restart requirement and no real render test.</p><p>Build prerequisite discovered during verification: remove duplicated import/component/interface declarations already present in the web working tree, preserving the complete PostDashboardView implementation and richer DTO declarations. Exclude separately vendored third-party source from the application&#39;s lint pass; do not change publishing behavior or third-party source.</p><p>Local sync 2026-11-09: retain remote text-brief generation and local image+prompt/reference generation when resolving stash conflicts. Never silently route image+prompt through text-only generation. Retain remote admin navbar access behavior and all locale keys. No new provider request, commit or push.</p>',11)])])}const h=o(i,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,h as default};
